			"Message": "feat(Grove/Transport): Implement Common Transport Adapter to bridge Grove transports\n\nThis commit introduces a new `TransportAdapter` that wraps Grove's concrete transport implementations (`GrpcTransport`, `IPCTransportImpl`, `WASMTransportImpl`) and presents them through the Common crate's `TransportStrategy` trait.\n\nThe adapter enables transport-agnostic code in the Land application by translating between:\n- Grove types (`TransportMessage`, `TransportStats`, `GrpcTransportError`)\n- Common DTOs (`UnifiedRequest`, `UnifiedResponse`, `TransportMetrics`, `TransportError`)\n\nKey functionality:\n- Implements `TransportStrategy` async trait from Common library\n- Provides bidirectional translation of transport types and metrics\n- Handles request/notification sending through the unified interface\n- Includes `From` implementations to convert Grove transport errors to Common errors\n- Adds a test case verifying adapter creation and type translation\n\nThis aligns with the architectural separation between Common (abstract traits) and Element implementations (concrete code), allowing Mountain and other components to interact with Grove transports through the Common abstraction layer.",
			"SHA": "6f5d8a14bc5a29731992d4b6fc7cb96ddc27aca5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-11T02:20:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡿⠀⠀⠀",
				68,
				25
			],
			"Message": "style(Grove): Apply consistent code formatting and indentation across codebase\n\nThis commit applies standardized Rust formatting throughout the Grove Element, establishing visual consistency across all modules. The changes are purely stylistic and do not affect runtime behavior.\n\nKey formatting changes:\n- Re-indent all doc comments to use proper 4-space indentation (previously mixed with no indentation)\n- Reorder imports in multiple modules for better organization (transport, WASM, binary, services)\n- Remove redundant blank lines in traits.rs\n- Simplify type annotations in test code (e.g., `anyhow::Result<()>` → `anyhow::Result<()>`)\n- Clean up debug formatting in SpineActionClient.rs\n- Reformat multi-line function calls and method chains for readability\n- Remove [profile] sections from Cargo.toml (profiles now inherited from workspace)\n\nAffected modules span the entire Grove architecture:\n- API: types.rs, vscode.rs\n- Binary: RuntimeBuildMod.rs, Entry.rs\n- Common: error.rs, traits.rs\n- Host: ExtensionManager.rs, Lifecycle.rs\n- Protocol: SpineActionClient.rs, SpineConnection.rs, mod.rs\n- Services: ConfigurationService.rs, mod.rs\n- Transport: GrpcTransport.rs, IpcTransport.rs, Strategy.rs, WASMTransport.rs, mod.rs\n- WASM: FunctionExport.rs, HostBridge.rs, ModuleLoader.rs, Runtime.rs\n- Library entry: lib.rs, main.rs\n\nThis follows the previous naming convention standardization (NC-05) and prepares Grove for consistent code review and tooling integration.",
			"SHA": "43b01096cc34a62c97d41141e40f87e1bd8126f8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-04T16:19:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				68,
